---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';

const updated = 'May 18, 2026';
const sections = [
  'What Cookies Are',
  'Technical Cookies',
  'Analytics Cookies',
  'We Do Not Use Advertising',
  'Cookie Table',
  'How to Manage Them',
  'Legal Basis and Consent',
  'Contact',
];
---

<Layout
  title="Cookie Policy | Lúmina W"
  description="Cookie Policy of Lúmina W S.A.S, technical and analytics cookies, how to manage and disable them."
>
  <article class="legal">
    <header class="legal__head">
      <p class="legal__kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
      <div class="legal__meta">
        <span><strong>Last updated:</strong> {updated}</span>
        <span><strong>Version:</strong> 1.0</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <p class="legal__intro">
      This Policy explains how
      <strong>Lúmina W S.A.S</strong> uses cookies and similar technologies on the
      site <em>luminaw.co</em>, for what purpose, for how long, and how you can
      disable them. It forms an integral part of the
      <a href="/en/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="legal__callout">
      <p>
        This English version is provided for convenience only. The legally
        binding text is the Spanish original at <a href="/cookies"
          >luminaw.co/cookies</a
        >. In case of any discrepancy, the Spanish version prevails.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal__body">
      <nav class="legal__toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
        <h2>Contents</h2>
        <ol>
          {
            sections.map((s, i) => (
              <li>
                <a href={`#sec-${String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}`}>{s}</a>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <div class="legal__content">
        <section id="sec-01" class="legal__section">
          <header class="legal__section-head">
            <span class="legal__num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
            <h2>What Cookies Are</h2>
          </header>
          <p>
            <strong>Cookies</strong> are small text files that a website saves in
            your browser or device when you visit it. They make it possible to remember
            information across pages or visits, keep your session active, remember
            preferences, or measure how the site is used in order to improve it.
          </p>
          <p>
            There are different types according to their origin (<strong
              >first party</strong
            > or <strong>third party</strong>), their duration (<strong
              >session</strong
            > or <strong>persistent</strong>) and their purpose (<strong
              >technical</strong
            >, <strong>analytics</strong>,
            <strong>advertising</strong>, etc.).
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="sec-02" class="legal__section">
          <header class="legal__section-head">
            <span class="legal__num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
            <h2>Technical Cookies</h2>
          </header>
          <p>
            These are <strong>strictly necessary</strong> for the site to function.
            They do not require prior consent under article 22 of the applicable regulations
            and the current SIC doctrine.
          </p>
          <p>We use technical cookies to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Keep the user session</strong> active during browsing.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Remember the decision</strong> about the cookie banner (accepted
              or rejected) so it is not asked on every visit.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Protection against CSRF</strong> and other threats in forms.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="sec-03" class="legal__section">
          <header class="legal__section-head">
            <span class="legal__num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
            <h2>Analytics Cookies</h2>
          </header>
          <p>
            They help us understand how the site is used in an
            <strong>aggregated and anonymous</strong> way (most visited pages, time
            on site, traffic sources), so we can make decisions about design, content,
            and performance.
          </p>
          <p>
            When we use <strong>Google Analytics</strong>, we do so with
            configurations that minimize the personal data collected: IP
            anonymization, disabling data sharing with other products, limited
            data retention.
          </p>
          <div class="legal__callout">
            <p>
              Analytics cookies are activated only
              <strong>with your express consent</strong>, given through the
              cookie banner. You can reject them without affecting how the site
              works.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="sec-04" class="legal__section">
          <header class="legal__section-head">
            <span class="legal__num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
            <h2>We Do Not Use Advertising</h2>
          </header>
          <p>
            Lúmina W <strong
              >does not use advertising cookies, retargeting, commercial
              profiling, or fingerprinting</strong
            > on this site. We also do not share browsing data with advertising networks.
          </p>
          <p>
            If in the future we adopt any marketing tool that requires
            additional cookies, we will update this Policy and request express
            consent before activating them.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="sec-05" class="legal__section">
          <header class="legal__section-head">
            <span class="legal__num" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
            <h2>Cookie Table</h2>
          </header>
          <p>
            The following list describes the cookies that may be found on the
            site, their origin, purpose, and approximate duration. The list may
            vary depending on the active tools.
          </p>
          <dl class="legal__defs">
            <div class="legal__def">
              <dt class="legal__def-term">cookie-consent</dt>
              <dd class="legal__def-desc">
                First party · technical · persistent (12 months). Remembers the
                user decision about the cookie banner.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="legal__def">
              <dt class="legal__def-term">_ga</dt>
              <dd class="legal__def-desc">
                Google Analytics · analytics · persistent (24 months).
                Distinguishes users.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="legal__def">
              <dt class="legal__def-term">_ga_*</dt>
              <dd class="legal__def-desc">
                Google Analytics 4 · analytics · persistent (24 months).
                Persists session state.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="legal__def">
              <dt class="legal__def-term">_gid</dt>
              <dd class="legal__def-desc">
                Google Analytics · analytics · session (24 hours). Identifies
                the user during the current visit.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <section id="sec-06" class="legal__section">
          <header class="legal__section-head">
            <span class="legal__num" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
            <h2>How to Manage Them</h2>
          </header>
          <h3>From the site</h3>
          <p>
            You can accept or reject analytics cookies through the banner that
            appears the first time you visit the site. The decision is recorded
            in the technical cookie
            <code>cookie-consent</code> for 12 months; you can change it at any time
            by deleting that cookie in your browser.
          </p>
          <h3>From the browser</h3>
          <p>Every browser lets you review, block, or delete cookies:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Chrome:</strong> Settings → Privacy and security → Cookies and
              other site data.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Firefox:</strong> Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Cookies
              and site data.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Safari:</strong> Preferences → Privacy → Manage website data.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Edge:</strong> Settings → Cookies and site permissions.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Google Analytics opt-out</h3>
          <p>
            You can install the official Google Analytics opt-out add-on:
            <a
              href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout</a
            >.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Important:</strong> blocking technical cookies may prevent some
            parts of the site from working correctly.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="sec-07" class="legal__section">
          <header class="legal__section-head">
            <span class="legal__num" aria-hidden="true">07</span>
            <h2>Legal Basis and Consent</h2>
          </header>
          <p>
            The use of technical cookies is supported by the
            <strong>legitimate interest</strong> of Lúmina W and by the need to provide
            the service requested by the user when entering the site.
          </p>
          <p>
            The use of analytics cookies is carried out only with the
            <strong>express consent of the user</strong>, under Law 1581 of 2012
            and Decree 1377 of 2013. Consent is revocable at any time without
            affecting the lawfulness of the prior processing.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="sec-08" class="legal__section">
          <header class="legal__section-head">
            <span class="legal__num" aria-hidden="true">08</span>
            <h2>Contact</h2>
          </header>
          <p>
            For questions about the use of cookies on this site or the exercise
            of rights related to personal data:
            <a href="mailto:contact@luminaw.co">contact@luminaw.co</a>.
          </p>
          <h3>Changes to this Policy</h3>
          <p>
            This Policy may be updated to reflect new tools or regulatory
            changes. Substantial changes will be announced through the site.
          </p>
        </section>

        <footer class="legal__foot">
          <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {updated}</p>
          <p>
            <strong>Contact:</strong>
            <a href="mailto:contact@luminaw.co">contact@luminaw.co</a>
            , Lúmina W S.A.S, Colombia.
          </p>
          <div class="legal__foot-links">
            <a href="/en/terms">Terms and Conditions</a>
            <a href="/en/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
            <a href="/en">Back to home</a>
          </div>
        </footer>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
